 "rule": "An overlay stays on the served grade only if it can be graded out of sample (as-of inputs exist for the labelled rows) AND, on every side where it fires, its paired within-(side, decision year) Spearman delta (overlay on minus off, scored object, rows with a MiLB block) has a CI95 lower bound above zero. Every other overlay leaves the grade: one with a measurable per-player statement becomes a labelled chip; one that cannot reorder players inside a side (a monotone per-side map, or a pricing-only map) is retired from the V2 grade because V2 sets the level from consensus values within (side, year) and prices from its own WAR line.",
